---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description={`How ${site.name} handles analytics, ads, cookies, and email. Nothing here asks a child for personal information.`} path="/privacy/">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>You can download a PDF without an account. These are coloring pages for a parent or a teacher to print.</p>
    <h2>What you do here</h2>
    <p>Reading a page and downloading a PDF does not ask for a name, an email, or a payment. If you email {site.email}, I get whatever you write, and I use it to write back.</p>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>If you allow cookies, the site may load Google Analytics 4 so I can see which sets get printed and which pages get opened. Cloudflare Web Analytics may also count visits without cookies. I use those counts to see how the site is used. I don't sell a profile of you.</p>
    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>The pages have spaces for Google ads. If an ad client is connected and you allow cookies, Google and its partners may use cookies to measure and personalize ads. You can say no on the banner and still download every PDF. Ad settings are also at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com">Google's ad settings</a>.</p>
    <h2>Pinterest</h2>
    <p>A lot of people arrive from Pinterest. If you allow cookies, a Pinterest tag may record that the visit came from a pin and that a PDF was the next step. The pin pictures are the coloring sets, so you can save a pile of pages.</p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>I wrote this for adults who print pages for children. It is not a service directed at children under 13. There are no child accounts, no chat, and no place for a child to send personal information. Please don't put a child's name or photo in an email unless you need to. A description of the page is enough.</p>
    <h2>Choices</h2>
    <p>The banner stores your choice in this browser. "No thanks" keeps analytics, the Pinterest tag, and ad cookies off. You can clear that choice by clearing site data for this domain.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this page: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
